                            <comment id="16698780" author="nsamelchev" created="Mon, 26 Nov 2018 11:03:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Most of the fails are assertions on failing coordinator node. I suggest to resolve &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5115&quot; title=&quot;Investigation of failing tests of coordinator node failure &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5115&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5115&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and take a look at the test at TC one more time. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16729690" author="githubbot" created="Thu, 27 Dec 2018 16:02:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user NSAmelchev opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5764&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5764&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10087&quot; title=&quot;IgniteClientReconnectMassiveShutdownTest.testMassiveServersShutdown1 is flaky in master&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-10087&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-10087&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; IgniteClientReconnectMassiveShutdownTest.testMassiveServersShutdown1 is flaky in master&lt;/p&gt;



